Hybrid or Agentic Chunking:
Based on how it’s implemented, this approach is often referred to as agentic or LLM-based, or simply adaptive chunking.
In this strategy, an intelligent agent dynamically decides which chunking strategy to apply based on the document type.
The system combines multiple chunking pipelines into one adaptive architecture.
This approach is commonly used in production-scale AI systems.

Remember:
There is no universal best chunking strategy.
The right approach depends on:
Document structure, Document length,
Type of content, Retrieval requirements

For example:
Blogs - Sentence chunking
Research papers - Semantic chunking
Codebases - Code-aware chunking
Reports - Page-level chunking

The best solution is to experiment with multiple strategies and evaluate retrieval quality.


